                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "30fe2ad0-950f-31f9-b1de-61d5627b8631",
                        "entry_id": "31f72f29-2a9e-3351-b31a-96e48823faf8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Angehöriger eines bettelnden Ordens, der im frühen 13. Jahrhundert durch Franziskus oder Franz von Assisi gegründet wurde"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b5a93de-5e82-4061-a74a-590fe703bf4a",
                                "sense_id": "30fe2ad0-950f-31f9-b1de-61d5627b8631",
                                "text": "Der Orden der Franziskaner wurde von Franziskus von Assisi (1181/82–1226) gegründet und 1209 durch Innozenz bestätigt."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eba8bf31-63a7-47ee-a48e-ebe5cd37fb54",
                                "sense_id": "30fe2ad0-950f-31f9-b1de-61d5627b8631",
                                "text": "Ein Franziskaner und ein Jesuit beteten im Kloster ihr Brevier."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "244621f1-15f5-4d45-8df5-b0a3721b855d",
                                "sense_id": "30fe2ad0-950f-31f9-b1de-61d5627b8631",
                                "text": "„Mit dem öffentlichen Auftreten von Mönchen aus den Bettelorden der Dominikaner und Franziskaner entwickelte sich auch die deutsche Predigt.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "48f892cf-8439-4c83-9d9a-9f2f1669159d",
                        "source_entry_id": "31f72f29-2a9e-3351-b31a-96e48823faf8",
                        "source_sense_id": "30fe2ad0-950f-31f9-b1de-61d5627b8631",
                        "target_lang_word": "Franciscan",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Franciscan",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "373aff12-ce2e-344e-a5f3-a3ff4638ceb4",
                                        "entry_id": "ad3ccecd-f658-3727-8602-a09e3eba4ff8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A friar of the religious order founded by Saint Francis of Assisi in 1209, now known as the Order of the Friars Minor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ffdf8584-6961-491f-b96d-1c1d21c32914",
                                                "sense_id": "373aff12-ce2e-344e-a5f3-a3ff4638ceb4",
                                                "text": "[O]ur old antient Purgatory pick-purſe, that vvas ſvvaged and covvled vvith a Franciſcan’s covvl, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b03bfd3-dae2-4bf7-8032-0a66bbb8e212",
                                                "sense_id": "373aff12-ce2e-344e-a5f3-a3ff4638ceb4",
                                                "text": "[A] ſilly iealous fellovve, that ſeeing his child nevv borne included in a kell [i.e., caul], thought ſure a Franciſcan that vſed to come to his houſe, vvas the father of it, it vvas ſo like a Friers Covvle, and therevpon threatned the Frier to kill him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9962a666-b0e5-44f9-9f68-0fdd43fa7f9d",
                                                "sense_id": "373aff12-ce2e-344e-a5f3-a3ff4638ceb4",
                                                "text": "We tried the Franciscans. The Jesuits. The Paulists. The Trappists. The Benedictines. […] Not one Franciscan in this city can make a positive identification of this bearded American priest. Every Franciscan we talked to was sure this man was not a member of their order. Yet he wears their habit and he heard confessions in one of their most important churches."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11a02035-97f4-4439-9122-7130cd3bced5",
                                                "sense_id": "373aff12-ce2e-344e-a5f3-a3ff4638ceb4",
                                                "text": "[T]he cities were growing rapidly, but the urban parish system was not, so when Franciscans entered the cities to preach, they encountered a substantial population in need not only of preaching but also of pastoral care."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d4682d0-174b-3859-845c-45200bd92fee",
                                        "entry_id": "ad3ccecd-f658-3727-8602-a09e3eba4ff8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A friar or nun of a religious order based on the rule of Francis of Assisi's original order, such as (Roman Catholicism) the Order of Friars Minor Capuchin (for men), Order of Friars Minor Conventual (men), Order of Saint Clare (women), or the Third Order of Saint Francis (men and women); or (Protestantism) certain orders in some Protestant churches, especially the Anglican Church and the Lutheran Church."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Franciscan",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5606e50c-da1d-36e1-bf18-57ff723bd832",
                                        "entry_id": "3b8586fe-6e64-3265-98c6-ee0d9dba6e54",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to Saint Francis of Assisi."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a0977b18-4c39-37aa-97d7-a166d998a290",
                                        "entry_id": "3b8586fe-6e64-3265-98c6-ee0d9dba6e54",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to (Roman Catholicism) the Order of the Friars Minor, or (Protestantism, Roman Catholicism) to another religious order based on the rule of Francis of Assisi's original order."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f591b969-d4ee-4ca2-b03f-390c7c6ff692",
                                                "sense_id": "a0977b18-4c39-37aa-97d7-a166d998a290",
                                                "text": "Holy Franciſcan Frier, brother, ho."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc509a29-9957-4850-a12d-4491c800ea0e",
                                                "sense_id": "a0977b18-4c39-37aa-97d7-a166d998a290",
                                                "text": "In his life time hee [Henry VII of England] founded the goodly Hoſpitall of the Sauoy, built ſixe religious Houſes for Franciſcan Friers, three of them for Obſeruants, and the other three for Conuentuals."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb1e46e3-29d0-47c1-8385-ecc595818474",
                                                "sense_id": "a0977b18-4c39-37aa-97d7-a166d998a290",
                                                "text": "And they vvho to be ſure of Paradiſe / Dying put on the vveeds of Dominic, / Or in Franciſcan think to paſs diſguis'd; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8ffa9d1-60c0-4fa2-aa6f-6a885470f969",
                                                "sense_id": "a0977b18-4c39-37aa-97d7-a166d998a290",
                                                "text": "So much for the firſt claſs of the Mendicants. The moſt numerous is the Serafic, or Franciſcan order, divided into as many ſpecies as pleaſed the fancies of the founders."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc27557f-30b5-45ab-ae93-c405019c8b95",
                                                "sense_id": "a0977b18-4c39-37aa-97d7-a166d998a290",
                                                "text": "There, a Franciscan friar named Andrés Ivars asked that Fr. Císcar hear his confession before the friar was executed be firing squad."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a2929eec-9b8c-4092-9aeb-943b089e467d",
                        "source_entry_id": "31f72f29-2a9e-3351-b31a-96e48823faf8",
                        "source_sense_id": "30fe2ad0-950f-31f9-b1de-61d5627b8631",
